          },
          "create_time": null,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              ""
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": null,
          "weight": 0.0,
          "metadata": {
            "is_visually_hidden_from_conversation": true
          },
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "client-created-root",
        "children": [
          "a_s01-m00"
        ]
      },
      "a_s01-m00": {
        "id": "a_s01-m00",
        "message": {
          "id": "a_s01-m00",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1788523800.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "In fibroblasts from Disease A patients we keep seeing a membrane protein piling up near the nucleus instead of reaching the cell surface. Could altered intracellular trafficking explain the phenotype, or am I over-reading one observation?"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": null,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {},
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "a_s01-sys",
        "children": [
          "a_s01-m01"
        ]
      },
      "a_s01-m01": {
        "id": "a_s01-m01",
        "message": {
          "id": "a_s01-m01",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1788523860.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "It's a reasonable hypothesis, but the same picture could come from several causes: slower delivery from the Golgi, faster internalisation, failure to recycle from endosomes, or simply more of the protein being made. Each predicts something different about where and how fast the protein moves, so the next step is to separate them."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {},
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "a_s01-m00",
        "children": [
          "a_s01-m02"
        ]
      },
      "a_s01-m02": {
        "id": "a_s01-m02",
        "message": {
          "id": "a_s01-m02",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1788523920.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "So I should treat 'trafficking defect' as a hypothesis to test, not a conclusion. What would most cleanly separate those explanations?"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": null,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {},
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "a_s01-m01",
        "children": [
          "a_s01-m03"
        ]
      },
      "a_s01-m03": {
        "id": "a_s01-m03",
        "message": {
          "id": "a_s01-m03",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1788523980.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Comparing total protein levels with the surface fraction rules expression in or out. Timing how quickly the protein reaches or leaves the surface separates delivery from recycling. Co-staining with compartment markers shows where it is stuck."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {},
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "a_s01-m02",
        "children": []
      }
    },
    "moderation_results": [],
    "current_node": "a_s01-m03",
    "conversation_id": "a_s01",
    "id": "a_s01"
